 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
-*   **Spatial Domain Zero-Padding:** If spatial domain zero-padding is too small in shear-based methods, data passes over the border and re-enters from the other side due to periodicity, an error amplified by consecutive shears. This method avoids this by not requiring large spatial domain zero-padding [S1].
-*   **Rounding Error:** Zero-padding can only be applied in discrete steps, so $K_0$ is rounded to the closest integer. For $K_0 > 50$, the deviation from the desired sampling distance $s_0$ is below $\pm 1.0\%$ [S1].
+*   **Spatial Domain Zero-Padding:** If spatial domain zero-padding is too small in shear-based methods, data passes over the border and re-enters from the other side due to periodicity, an error amplified by consecutive shears [S1]. This method avoids this by not requiring large spatial domain zero-padding [S1].
+*   **Rounding Error:** Zero-padding can only be applied in discrete steps, so $K_0^{pad}$ is rounded to the closest integer [S1]. For $K_0^{pad} > 50$, the deviation from the desired sampling distance $s'$ is below $\pm 1.0\%$ [S1].
 
